    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a potent offensive alignment, headlined by **Yordan Alvarez** (82.58) and **Junior Caminero** (80.71). **Yordan Alvarez** is a locked-in start, benefiting from a favorable matchup against Yesavage and a massive 0.476 xwOBA that anchors the middle of the order. Meanwhile, **Junior Caminero** is positioned to feast on Hughes; he carries a significant 14% park-factor boost, making him our highest-rated utility option. Furthermore, the combination of **Trea Turner** (76.02) and **Kyle Schwarber** (76.87) against the left-handed Palmquist provides an ideal stack at the top of the order. Both benefit from significant SP skill ratings and the advantage of leading off against a pitcher with a 4.49 xERA, driving their efficiency well into the \"Strong\" territory.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today's roster involved **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (47.32), who was the first cut from the active lineup. While his elite speed profile typically makes him a priority for the Zebras, he is facing an elite arm in Skubal (2.67 xERA). The matchup risk\u2014specifically the 19% downgrade for SP skill and a 15% negative platoon split\u2014pushed him just below the threshold required to displace **Nelson Velazquez** (49.05). Elsewhere, **Lars Nootbaar** (67.77) serves as a high-value play; despite a lower base projection, he enjoys a massive 19% SP skill advantage against V\u00e1squez, making him an underrated engine for our daily offensive output. \n\nWe are monitoring the risk profile of **Christian Yelich** (53.66), whose start is predicated on a strong platoon advantage against Jones. However, owners should note the elite catcher framing (1.86s pop time) behind the plate today, which slightly tempers his floor. We have successfully avoided the basement, with players like **Dillon Dingler** (39.14) and **Pedro Ramirez** (36.23) correctly benched for falling below the 40.0 efficiency floor. As we look to preserve game caps, the focus remains on high-leverage starts like **Kazuma Okamoto** (59.90), who\u2014despite a neutral platoon\u2014should capitalize on a 14% SP skill boost against Wesneski.",
